#. Source: input/pagecontent/adapting.md:9
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust-phw/adapting.html
#: input/pagecontent/adapting.md:9
msgid "For more on layers of knowledge representation and how they are used in WHO’s SMART Guidelines approach, see <a0>WHO’s SMART Guidelines</a0> and this <a1>Lancet article</a1>00038-8/fulltext)."
msgstr "有关知识表示的各层及其在世卫组织（WHO）SMART 指南方法中的应用，详见<a0>世卫组织（WHO）SMART 指南</a0>及这篇 <a1>Lancet 文章</a1>00038-8/fulltext)。"

#. Source: input/pagecontent/adapting.md:1
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust-phw/adapting.html
#: input/pagecontent/adapting.md:1
msgid "The following page provides a reference to resources that can guide countries in adapting the guidelines for country use."
msgstr "以下页面提供参考资源，可指导各国针对本国使用对指南进行适配。"

#. Source: input/pagecontent/adapting.md:13
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust-phw/adapting.html
#: input/pagecontent/adapting.md:13
msgid "The fourth layer (L4: Executable—reference applications and services) focuses on software applications and services within a digital ecosystem. It is intended to include executable reference software that accurately represents the intentions, operational, and functional requirements of the WHO recommendations; addresses user and health system needs; and comprises machine-readable data and calculations within interoperability standards, as documented in the L1–L3 layers. As a fully functional application, it is intended to serve as a generic starting point, ready to be localised to the specific operational context of the users, population, and health system within which it is deployed. Additional products at this layer include terminology services to support consistent data representation for interoperability; reusable software libraries including software development kits; application programming interfaces; and function as a service to support updates to FHIR content and capabilities across subscribed digital systems."
msgstr "第四层（L4：可执行——参考应用程序和服务）侧重于数字生态系统中的软件应用程序和服务。该层旨在包含可执行的参考软件，这些软件准确体现世卫组织（WHO）建议的意图、操作需求和功能需求；满足用户和卫生系统的需求；并按照 L1–L3 层所记录的内容，在互操作性标准内包含机器可读的数据和计算。作为功能完备的应用程序，它旨在充当通用的起点，可随时根据其部署所在的用户、人群和卫生系统的具体运行环境进行本地化。该层的其他产品包括：支持一致数据表示以实现互操作性的术语服务；可复用的软件库（包括软件开发工具包）；应用程序编程接口；以及功能即服务，以支持在已订阅的各数字系统中更新 FHIR 内容和功能。"

#. Source: input/pagecontent/adapting.md:11
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust-phw/adapting.html
#: input/pagecontent/adapting.md:11
msgid "The standards-based technical artifacts in this implementation guide are at the third layer of knowledge representation (L3: Machine-readable recommendations). It provides code necessary for software developers to incorporate standardised logic from WHO guidelines into digital systems, testable for conformance to standards including fidelity to recommendations. A standards-based technical implementation guide builds on operational (L2) by mapping L2 content to value sets and Health Level Seven International Fast Healthcare Interoperability Resources (FHIR) standards. Alongside data standards from L2, this allows for semantic and syntactic interoperability at scale. The logic derived from guidelines, which might include clinical decision support and calculations for performance indicators, which may be encoded into Clinical Quality Language (CQL). This ensures that key indicators can be consistently extracted to support patient care, as well as case surveillance and programme monitoring. The machine-readable representations in this implementation guide are intended for adaptation into countries’ digital health service delivery and reporting systems. Digital solutions comprising L3 machine-readable recommendations may then be testable for conformance to interoperability standards."
msgstr "本实施指南中基于标准的技术工件处于知识表示的第三层（L3：机器可读建议）。该层提供软件开发人员所需的代码，用于将世卫组织（WHO）指南中的标准化逻辑纳入数字系统，并可测试其是否符合标准，包括是否忠实于建议。基于标准的技术实施指南以操作层（L2）为基础，将 L2 内容映射到值集和 Health Level Seven International 快速医疗互操作性资源（FHIR）标准。结合 L2 的数据标准，可实现大规模的语义和句法互操作性。从指南中派生的逻辑（可能包括临床决策支持和绩效指标计算）可以用临床质量语言（CQL）进行编码。这可确保一致地提取关键指标，以支持患者护理以及病例监测和规划监测。本实施指南中的机器可读表示旨在供各国调整后纳入其数字健康服务提供和报告系统。包含 L3 机器可读建议的数字解决方案随后可接受互操作性标准符合性测试。"

#. Source: input/pagecontent/adapting.md:5
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust-phw/adapting.html
#: input/pagecontent/adapting.md:5
msgid "This implementation guide provides the generic content required in digital systems, independently of a specific software application and with the intention that countries can adapt it to meet local needs."
msgstr "本实施指南提供数字系统所需的通用内容，不依赖于特定的软件应用程序，旨在让各国能够对其进行适配以满足本地需求。"

#. Source: input/pagecontent/adapting.md:3
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust-phw/adapting.html
#: input/pagecontent/adapting.md:3
msgid "To implement WHO recommendations in country settings, governments must interpret and then adapt the content in line with local policies, procedures, and digital tools."
msgstr "要在国家环境中实施世卫组织（WHO）的建议，各国政府必须根据本地政策、程序和数字工具对内容进行解读和适配。"

#. Source: input/pagecontent/adapting.md:7
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust-phw/adapting.html
#: input/pagecontent/adapting.md:7
msgid "WHO guidelines articulate and endorse rigorously tested recommendations for health interventions to be adopted within country programs. When applied correctly and consistently, guideline recommendations save lives. To ensure that countries can effectively benefit from digital health investments, the SMART Guidelines approach is intended to facilitate the accurate reflection of WHO’s clinical, public health and data use guidelines in the digital systems that countries are adopting."
msgstr "世卫组织（WHO）指南阐明并认可经过严格检验的卫生干预措施建议，供各国规划采用。正确且一致地应用指南建议可以挽救生命。为确保各国能够切实受益于数字健康投资，SMART 指南方法旨在促进世卫组织（WHO）的临床、公共卫生和数据使用指南在各国所采用的数字系统中得到准确体现。"

